    "commit": "0e237755513e51b9d429de6285d9b833e3e4ac03",
    "commit_message": "Add pull-based VM auto-deploy so merging a PR reaches production without a manual SSH (#63)\n\nMerging a PR on GitHub only ever updated main - nothing on this VM ever\nchecked GitHub, so every backend fix required the Captain to SSH in and\ngit pull by hand. Confirmed there was no webhook receiver, no self-hosted\nGitHub Actions runner, and no auto-deploy script anywhere in this repo\nbefore this one; the frontend (lcars-portal) already closes this loop via\nVercel, this closes the other half.\n\ndeploy/auto-deploy.sh (run every 5 minutes by the paired timer):\n- Refuses to touch a dirty working tree - a manual in-progress change on\n  the VM always wins over automation, and it aborts loudly rather than\n  pulling over it.\n- Fast-forward only. Never merges, never rebases, never resolves a\n  conflict, never pushes - if history has diverged it stops and surfaces\n  that rather than guessing.\n- lcars-portal/ changes trigger an actual `npm ci && npm run build` before\n  restarting that service (a Next.js production server is pre-compiled -\n  a bare restart would keep serving the old build); every other\n  configured service in auto-deploy-services.conf restarts unconditionally\n  on any successful pull, since mapping specific changed files to specific\n  services is fragile. Everything else on this VM (delivery-reconciler,\n  hq-evolution, etc.) needs no restart at all - those are oneshot jobs\n  that pick up new code on their own next scheduled run automatically.\n\nauto-deploy-services.conf ships as a best-guess starting list, explicitly\nflagged as unverified: while building this, found real drift between this\nrepo's deploy/*.service filenames and what's actually live (this repo's\nxo-bot.service file names a unit that isn't what runs -\ntelegram-bots/xo/app.py's own /restart_bots command targets tg-xo.service\ninstead, and separately references a live starfleet-slack-bot.service\nwith no matching file in deploy/ at all). A wrong name in this list just\nlogs a warning and is otherwise harmless - it never restarts a\ndifferently-named unit by mistake, but the Captain still needs to confirm\nthis list against `systemctl list-units` on the actual VM.\n\ntests/test_auto_deploy.sh: 5 functional tests (run directly, no pytest\nshell-test harness in this repo) against throwaway git repo fixtures,\nnever the real VM - up-to-date no-op, backend-only pull with no npm\nbuild, lcars-portal change triggers rebuild, dirty tree aborts cleanly,\ndiverged history aborts without corrupting the local branch. npm and\nsystemctl are stubbed, never invoked for real.\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Er5eaMeHeZQdPoauqYAkVA\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>",
